Day 29 – Topological Sort (DFS)
Problem Solved
Topological Sort (GFG)
Concepts Used
Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)
DFS Traversal
Stack
Dependency Ordering
Graph Traversal
Approach
Build adjacency list.
Perform DFS from every unvisited node.
Visit all neighbours first.
Push current node into stack after DFS completes.
Reverse the stack to get Topological Ordering.
Key Insight

Nodes are added to the stack only after all their dependencies have been processed.

This guarantees that every prerequisite appears before the dependent node in the final ordering.

Complexity
Time: O(V + E)
Space: O(V)
